# source as shell and EXECUTE any backticked prose in it as commands. Python reads this line as a
# no-op string; sh/bash re-execs the file under python3 before reaching any other line.
# Statically enforced for every python mr-* tool by mr-selfcheck.
"""mr-tester-ab — the tester A/B experiment: shadow testers, replay, ledger.

WHAT IT MEASURES
----------------
On an eligible slice the tier-policy tester writes the gating tests as always. Extra tester runs
(the arms: a model and an effort each, plus one replicate) write tests blind from the same prompt
and the same tree. Their tests never enter the repo. This tool keeps each arm's tests under a
local ref, replays them against recorded snapshots of the builder's implementation, and records
which arm's unedited test flipped on a game-code change. A judge that is not an arm rules which
flips are real defects.

SAFETY CONTRACT
---------------
  * `enabled` in mr-tester-ab.config.json must be the JSON value true. Otherwise every command
    prints `AB-SKIP disabled` and reads and writes nothing else.
  * Every command exits 0 (`--selftest` exits 1 on failure). On a skip or an error it prints
    `AB-SKIP <reason>` and the slice proceeds as it does without the experiment.
  * No command starts a model session. `plan` prints Agent calls for the builder to issue.
  * No command reads or writes a stop flag, a lock of the loop, or a merge.
  * It addresses the directory it ships in (config, ledger, side files), so a copy in a
    temporary directory is a sandbox.

FILES
-----
  mr-tester-ab.config.json   tracked. Arms, eligibility, caps, runner commands.
  mr-tester-ab.jsonl         the ledger. Append-only, one JSON object per line, written under
                             flock. Every row has v, kind, slice, ts. Gitignored.
  tester-ab/<slice>/         manifest, shadow reports, failure output. Gitignored.
  <cache_root>/<slice>/<id>/ one plain export of the tree per shadow run; not a git worktree.
  <cache_root>/scratch/      the one directory every replay runs in; <cache_root>/target is the
                             cargo target directory they share.
  refs/mr-ab/<slice>/<name>  in the game repo, local: the snapshots (base, g1, g2, m, end) and
                             each shadow's tests (its label).

LEDGER ROWS (kind)
------------------
  assignment  milestone, tier, labels {label: arm}, prompt_sha256, base_ref, tester_md_sha,
              arms_planned, skipped (null or the reason)
  run         label, arm, role (primary | shadow | replicate | followup), twin, session,
              agent_id, tool_use_id, model_observed, effort_observed, cli_version, started,
              duration_s, calls, bash_blocked, tokens, cost_usd, status (ok | failed |
              contaminated | arm-mismatch), leak, tests_ref, files, non_test_files, tests, test_loc
  snap        name (base | g1 | g2 | m | end), sha, source (tool | derived)
  exec        label, snap, test_id, criterion_tag, result (pass | fail | no-compile | not-run),
              runtime_ms, run_n, ported
  claim       claim_id, label, type (base | spec), test, where, text, text_sha
  candidate   candidate_id, type (lens-caught | escape | base | spec | open-fail), label,
              test_id or claim_id, snap_fail, snap_pass, game_diff, scope (in | out),
              handed_in_session. The latest row of a (label, test_id or claim_id) stands.
  quality     label, no_compile_files, flaky, brittle, test_loc, tests, loc_per_criterion,
              dup_assert_lines, runtime_ms, bloat_usd. The latest row of a label stands.
  mutants     label, generated, caught, missed, unviable, timeouts, wall_s, status (ok | budget |
              error | no-tests). A reported measure; nothing gates on it.
  slice       status (scored | degraded | void), arms_ok, area, added_cost_usd,
              cumulative_added_usd. The latest row of a slice stands.

COMMANDS
--------
  eligible <slice> [<repo>]   `yes <cap bump usd>` or `no <reason>`. For mr-spawn.
  plan <slice> --prompt <file> [--worktree <dir>] [--tier <t>] [--milestone <m>]
                              Snapshot the slice worktree as `base`, export it once per shadow,
                              write each shadow's prompt into its export, and print the Agent
                              calls. A second call for the same slice prints the same calls.
  collect <slice>             After the calls return: keep each shadow's new and changed files
                              as a commit under its ref, price the runs from their transcripts,
                              flag contamination, arm mismatch and leak, copy the reports, delete
                              the exports the manifest registered, print the claim digest.
  score <slice> [--end]       Replay each arm's tests at every recorded snapshot (base: claimed
                              tests only; m: twice), derive candidates and the per-arm quality
                              and seeded-defect rows. `--end` first records the game repo's
                              default-branch head as `end`. Runs what is missing; under a flock.
  status                      What is planned, collected, scored and spent; stale exports.
  --selftest                  Fixtures against temporary directories and a toy test runner.
                              Prints `TESTER-AB-SELFTEST-OK <n>`.
"""

